James asked how to create a highlighted document from a comparison of two Word documents, seeking to emphasize changes. I provided detailed steps for both Microsoft Word and potential workarounds for Google Docs, including the use of the "Compare Documents" feature and third-party tools. He later inquired about simplifying the display of changes in Word, specifically wanting to highlight changes without annotations. I explained how to accept/reject changes, adjust track changes settings, and save a PDF without comments. I also suggested options to display highlighted changes only, while ensuring flexibility for his document presentation.
